2026-10-15: ③ line cache (rimCached) full audit — conclusion: no bug (with evidence chain)
- Background: after the v-memo content-mixing bug was rolled back, a full audit of rendering-performance ③ (MessageContent.vue rimCached line cache) was run for similar hazards
- Verification: check_rimcache_behavior.mjs 18/18 (pure-functionality/reference stability/clear boundaries/edge inputs/multi-instance isolation); check_rimcache_updatepath.mjs (real Vue createRenderer update path: unchanged lines skip patchProp, changed lines update, Fragment multi-line delta=1); SFC compile confirms lineCache lives in setup() (one per instance); runtime-core patchElement source confirms the `next!==prev` skip logic
- Conclusion: rimCached is a pure function mapping (key = line text → HTML); same input always yields the same output, so content mixing is structurally impossible; the essential difference from v-memo: v-memo caches the whole vnode in shared slots (can mix), rimCached caches a text→HTML pure mapping (same input → same output)
- Scripts archived: .pebble/_tmp_verify/check_rimcache_behavior.mjs, check_rimcache_updatepath.mjs

2026-10-15: Segment-level v-memo freeze rolled back (thinking/body segments cross-contaminated content)
- Symptom: all thinking cards showed the same content (segment 0) and all body cards the same (segment 1); only the last segment was normal
- Investigation: agent_chat.db / sessions.db data intact (segments differ, no pollution) → frontend rendering bug
- Root cause: segment-level freeze v-memo misuse — inside v-for, Vue shares fixed cache slots across ALL list items (compiler output _withMemo(deps, fn, _cache, 0/1/2); runtime withMemo returns the old vnode without re-rendering when memo matches). After reload, every segment except the last has isFrozen=true → identical memo values → later segments all hit the first segment's cache (reasoning segments all show segment 0 / text all segment 1 / tool all segment 2); during streaming, unfinalized segments have memo constantly false → content updates also skipped (stuck at first-frame content, jumping at finalization)
- Evidence: Vue 3.5.39 compiler output + runtime-core withMemo/isMemoSame source (.pebble/_tmp_verify/check_vmemo_compile.mjs, check_vmemo_runtime.mjs archived)
- Rollback: MessageBubble.vue removed three v-memo usages + the isFrozen function (v-for restored without index); ① streaming throttle + ③ line cache kept (independent and safe); vue-tsc passes; verify_render_perf.mjs 21/21 (part 2 changed to rollback assertions)
- Note: v-memo inside v-for cannot implement "per-item freezing" (shared slots); segment-level freezing needs child components + shouldUpdateComponent-style mechanisms instead

