2026-10-03: WebSocket message-size limit removed + reconnect-state fix (image-send stuck at "loading")
- Case: after sending an image the UI stuck at "Agent is responding..." forever; the message never reached the server (sessions.db evidence: that conversation fa716f99 message_count=0, no message rows, title not updated — handle_prompt_submit never called)
- Root cause: gateway/ws_server.py's websockets.serve() had no max_size, using the websockets 16.0 library default of 1 MiB; images upload as base64 (4/3 inflation) → an original image above ~768KB exceeded the whole-message limit → the server closed the connection at the protocol layer with 1009 (MESSAGE_TOO_BIG) and dropped the message (never delivered to the handler); compounded by a frontend state gap: on disconnect onStatus didn't clear streaming → the UI stayed stuck and couldn't resend
- Fix 1 (backend core): ws_server.py serve() + max_size=None (removes the per-message size limit entirely; websockets officially supports None = disabled)
- Fix 2 (frontend defense): gatewayClient.ts sendMessage returns boolean (not connected/exception → false, no silent drops); gateway.ts new failPendingStream() — on onStatus(false) while streaming, or sendMessage false, marks the unfinished stream as Error (Connection lost / Not connected) and resets streaming/agentMsgId/streamRef
- Verification: isolated test (random port, no project services involved) — default config rejects a 2MiB message with 1009 (reproduced), max_size=None config sends/receives 2MiB fine (fix works); py_compile passes; vue-tsc --noEmit 0 errors
- Notes: the frontend still keeps the 10MB/20-file attachment cap (product design, unchanged); LLM API body limits (e.g. DeepSeek 48MiB) are downstream constraints; API errors display normally when exceeded
